# Test: `ze doctor` on a config with main-table static routes and no `fib { }`
#       block reports nothing about a missing FIB writer.
# VALIDATES: spec-connected-static-reach-the-locrib, owner decision 2026-09-06 --
#            the FIB plugin is AUTO-LOADED when static is used, so a config an
#            operator could commit before main-table routes moved to the Loc-RIB
#            is not diagnosed as unroutable after it.
# PREVENTS: the data-plane writer check (plugin-dataplane-writer) going back to refusing every static
#           config that does not name a data-plane backend, which is what commit
#           125979ea99 shipped and what this replaces.
#
# The sibling case, a data plane no plugin programs, is
# TestDataPlaneWriterRowMatchesRefusal
# (internal/component/plugin/doctor/check_reload_dataplane_test.go): it needs a
# data plane no writer programs, which the daemon
# refuses to load, so it is not reachable from a config `ze doctor` accepts.

tmpfs=static-no-fib.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
static {
    table default {
        route 10.0.0.0/8 {
            next { hop 192.168.1.1 { } }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json config static-no-fib.conf
expect=stdout:contains=diagnostics
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-no-dataplane-writer
